-"""THE FINAL SWITCH, carried by the server (lane FINAL-SWITCH, 2026-09-26).
-
-Arman's ruling (2026-09-26): *"I don't want to do this one org at a time. We will switch
-everything over once we know it works and it's done. Old gone, new in place."*
-
-The switch itself lives in the database (matrx-frontend
-``migrations/campaign/finalswitch_one_press_switches_every_organization_and_one_undo_reverses_it.sql``):
-
-* ``platform.final_switch_readiness()`` — every organization's readiness, one answer.
-* ``platform.final_switch_press(note, copy_again)`` — ONE transaction: Data tables for every
-  organization, agent context, the platform values, the scope screens (their lane's step), the
-  Data page, the older write doors closed to clients, the trim paused, one press record.
-* ``platform.final_switch_undo(note, accept_not_carried)`` — the same steps backwards.
-
-The database decides who may press (a platform administrator, signed in, from a page, in the
-admin lane) and refuses while anything is not ready. This module adds the two things SQL cannot
-do and a browser request cannot wait for:
-
-1. **Copy again where it clears something** — the mover's COPY rerun
-   (:func:`matrx_records.movers.copy_again.copy_again`, the same one the settings card's button
-   runs) for every organization whose readiness says copying again clears a difference. It is
-   Python and it is long.
-2. **The long transaction** — the press measures every organization twice and re-syncs every
-   copy; a browser request is cut at 8 s. So the press runs here, AS THE PERSON: their own verified
-   token's claims (:func:`aidream.db.acting_as.build_user_claims`), the page's ``Origin``, the admin
-   lane (this is an admin mount), a statement timeout of ten minutes. Nothing about the person is
-   invented here; a request without them never reaches the database's press.
-
-3. **The context copy** (coordinator 2026-09-27, after SCOPES-TAILS' ``own_words_copied``) — Step 1
-   covers it too: for every organization readiness names in ``needs_context_copy``, the follow's own
-   pass for that one organization (:meth:`ContextFollow.drain` with its id: it claims the edits
-   waiting for it, runs the same copy ``runner.py --copy-context --apply`` runs, and releases the
-   claims when it fails), then the parity measurement again for that organization (the same sweep
-   and record ``scripts/context_parity.py --every-type --record`` writes), then readiness read back.
-   It runs only on a server whose tag copy is not cut off by the database's 30-second clock
-   (aidream 991ff424b5, :func:`context_copy_capability`); on any other it is refused by name.
-
-The whole press, the undo and the press again were proven by calling these same functions against
-the dev clone (the one-shot rehearsal runner retired 2026-10-02 once the switch was done).
-"""
-
-from __future__ import annotations
-
-import json
-import logging
-import time
-import uuid
-from collections.abc import Awaitable, Callable
-from dataclasses import dataclass, field
-from typing import Any
-
-logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
