-"""The user-defined tables (``workbench.udt_*``) → Table / Record / Field / Value / Relation.
-
-This is the store behind the ``/data`` page and the ``/lists`` pages, and it is the one a
-person would notice most: 164 datasets, 903 fields, 5,372 rows and 7,854 row versions on
-the main database when this mover was written. It is also the closest thing the platform
-already has to the new model — a Table of typed columns with rows and history — so the
-mapping is almost entirely a rename.
-
-``workbench.udt_datasets`` → **Table**
-    ``id`` → the Table record's id (CUT-4). ``table_name`` → the name and the slug,
-    ``description`` kept (the Table record carries no row-access word, so none is copied),
-    ``row_ordering_config.enabled`` → ``row_order``
-    (``manual`` when a hand order is on, ``sorted`` otherwise) and its ``default_sort``
-    → the Table's ``default_sort``. ``display`` is ``list``: a dataset is a grid.
-    ``project_id`` / ``task_id`` / ``workbook_id`` are FK CONTAINMENT and would be an
-    OWNED containment (CUT-9) — but only if the parent is itself a Record in the store,
-    and a project is not, so each one is reported by id rather than dropped.
-
-``workbench.udt_dataset_fields`` → **Field**
-    ``id`` → the Field record's id, ``table_id`` → ``entity_definition_id``,
-    ``field_name`` → ``key``, ``display_name`` → ``label``, ``data_type`` → the behavior
-    and its modifiers, ``is_required`` → ``required``, ``field_order`` → ``sort``,
-    ``default_value`` → ``default``. ``validation_rules`` is the one that is NOT a
-    rename: the store refuses a constraint written into a field's config by name
-    (*"a constraint is a Rule"*), so each rule becomes an attached Rule of a kind the
-    store can execute, and one it cannot is reported rather than quietly dropped.
-
-``workbench.udt_dataset_rows`` → **Record**, ``id`` → the Record's id, ``table_id`` →
-    the Table, and the row's ``data`` jsonb becomes the Record's Values, one per column.
-
-``workbench.udt_dataset_row_versions`` → **the Values' versions**, replayed oldest first
-    so the store counts to the same number the old table recorded. This table is the
-    reason the old store has TWO version systems (``history.row_versions`` holds nothing
-    for it) and the move collapses them into the one the new store keeps.
-
-``workbench.udt_structured_lists`` / ``_items`` → **a Table of choices and its Records**
-    An option set already IS a Table of records in the new model (FLD-5), so a structured
-    list becomes a Table with ``display: list`` and each item becomes one of its Records.
