-themselves, one seat at a time, and had no way from any screen to open it for
-the people they work with.
-
-THE RULING (lane NAV-FIX, 19 September). There is ONE switch and it belongs to
-the ORGANIZATION: ``platform.feature_knob`` ``custom/system_enabled``, set once
-on the unified data ramp screen by an owner or an administrator, for everybody
-in that organization. Every surface reads that and nothing else — the pages
-(``matrx-frontend/lib/knobs/unifiedDataCampaign.ts``), the Records entry in the
-sidebar, this package's server gateway, and this package's agent tool. There is
-no per-person rung anywhere on the path, and this module is where that is true:
-``platform.knob_resolve`` is called with an organization and NO user, so a
-``platform.knob_override`` scoped to one person cannot decide it even if
-somebody writes one.
-
-WHAT THE AGENT TOOL USED TO ASK, and why it broke. It resolved
-``custom/code_paths_enabled`` — the campaign's process-wide code kill switch —
-*with a user*, and relied on a per-person override row to raise it. That knob's
-person rung was removed with the rest of the second switch, so the tool then
-refused everybody. It was the wrong question from the start: whether a
-person may drive the record store is the same question as whether their
-organization keeps its data there, and it now asks that one.
-
-WHY IT DOES NOT RAISE. A switch that cannot be read must read as OFF — an
-unreachable database turning a half-built store ON for everybody is the failure
-that matters. So every failure here answers ``False`` and SAYS SO, naming the
-knob and the remedy, because nothing fails silently.
-"""
-
-from __future__ import annotations
-
-import logging
-
-logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
-
-#: THE knob. *Does this organization keep its data in the unified record store?*
-STORE_SWITCH = ("custom", "system_enabled")
-
-#: Set for every organization by the final switch's press: its tables live in the store now.
-TABLES_MOVED = ("data_tables", "older_tables_moved")
-
-
-def _truthy(raw: object) -> bool:
-    return str(raw).strip().strip('"').lower() in {"true", "t", "1"}
-
-
-#: The remedy, in the words of the screen that does it. One sentence, no knob key.
-#:
-#: STORE-ON 2026-09-23 (owner ruling): the record store is ON for every organization by
-#: default, so this stopped being a setup step somebody had not got to and became a switch
-#: somebody in the organization moved. "turns it back on" is the honest verb.
-TURN_IT_ON = (
-    "An owner or an administrator of this organization turns the record store back on, "
-    "for everybody in it, on the unified data ramp screen."
-)
-
-
-async def store_is_on(organization_id: str | None) -> tuple[bool, str]:
-    """``(on?, why)`` for one organization. Unreadable, or no organization, is OFF.
-
-    The organization is the ONLY thing passed to ``platform.knob_resolve``. Passing a
-    user as well is what made this a per-person switch, and a per-person rung on the one
-    switch is what this lane exists to remove.
-    """
-    if not organization_id:
-        return False, (
-            "no organization was named, and the record store is one organization's "
-            "decision — so there is nothing here to reach. Nothing was read and nothing "
-            "was written."
-        )
-
-    from matrx_orm import call_function
-
-    from matrx_records.principal import records_database
-
-    try:
-        raw = await call_function(
-            records_database(),
-            "platform",
-            "knob_resolve",
-            *STORE_SWITCH,
-            organization_id,
-        )
-    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 — announced, never silent
-        logger.warning(
-            "matrx_records: could not read platform.feature_knob custom/system_enabled "
-            "for organization %s: %s",
-            organization_id,
-            exc,
-        )
-        return False, (
-            f"the record store's switch could not be read ({exc}), so nothing was read "
-            "and nothing was written. This is not a refusal — it is a switch we could "
-            f"not check. {TURN_IT_ON}"
-        )
-
-    if _truthy(raw):
-        return True, "this organization keeps its data in the unified record store."
-    # AFTER THE PRESS THE STORE IS THE ONLY SYSTEM (lane POST-PRESS-SENTENCES, 2026-10-01; chair
-    # ruling on safety net C15). Once an organization's tables have moved
-    # (``data_tables/older_tables_moved``, which the final switch's press sets for every
-    # organization), its record-store switch means nothing: births and writes go to the store.
-    # The database's ``custom.store_is_open`` answers the same way, so the two never disagree.
-    try:
-        moved = await call_function(
-            records_database(), "platform", "knob_resolve", *TABLES_MOVED, organization_id
-        )
-    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 — announced; the switch's own answer stands
-        logger.warning(
-            "matrx_records: could not read data_tables/older_tables_moved for organization %s: %s",
-            organization_id,
-            exc,
-        )
-        moved = None
-    if _truthy(moved):
-        return True, (
-            "this organization's tables moved to the unified record store, which is now the only "
-            "place they live."
-        )
-    return False, (
-        "this organization has its record store switched off, so there is nothing here to "
-        f"read or write. {TURN_IT_ON}"
-    )
