-"""A COPY OF AN OLDER TABLE OPENS AS THE SHEET IT ALWAYS WAS (lane DATA-V2-FACE-2, 2026-09-24).
-
-THE USE CASE. Rincon Plumbing Co kept its service calls in the older data tables, where every
-table simply WAS a sheet and nobody ever saved a view. The mover copies "Service Calls" into the
-record store. The office manager opens it on /data-v2 and must see the Sheet, not a chooser of
-Grid · Kanban · Calendar · Gallery · Sheet. Owner, 2026-09-24: "for something like my data tables,
-which are predetermined with a default view of 'Sheet' I want to see … it just shows them the way it
-should in the default view."
-
-RED on the pre-lane mover: a copy with no older saved views and no hand-set row order got NO
-default view at all (the mover made one only to hold a row order), so records-ui seeded a plain
-"All records" grid and showed the chooser.
-
-The store is simulated in memory at the SQL the mover sends (platform.saved_view rows and the
-``custom.view_declare`` door, which keeps ``moved_from`` at birth under every body it has had). The
-live proof is the clone rehearsal of the data repair beside this change.
