-"""Copying again carries what the older side REMOVED into the copy — lane MOVER-DELETIONS.
-
-THE USE CASE. Ridgeline HVAC's dispatcher keeps "Service Calls" in admin's Workspace; the
-organization has not pressed its Data tables switch, so the older table is the truth and its copy in
-the new system is what the switch will show. After the copy the dispatcher, on the older screens:
-
-* deletes a duplicate job (the older store deletes the row),
-* deletes the "Truck" column nobody fills in (the older store deletes the column),
-* takes "Duct cleaning" off the "Job types" pick list the Job type column chooses from (the older
-  list editor rewrites the list's choices, so the old choice is deleted),
-* stops sharing the table with test@test.com (an older share names a person; SHARE-PEOPLE-ONLY),
-* removes the colour rule that painted Dana's jobs red.
-
-Before this lane Copy again only ever ADDED, so every one of those stayed live on the copy and the
-switch brought it back: the duplicate job in the grid, the Truck column on the page, "Duct cleaning"
-in every picker, test@test.com able to open the table. Now:
-
-1. the settings card's check "Nothing removed from an older table or list is still on its copy"
-   names them, with ``copy_again_clears`` so the card offers Copy again (the shares check counts the
-   shares, and now says copying again clears the ones the mover carried);
-2. Copy again archives each on the copy through the store's own doors — never a hard delete of a
-   record — and says so in its sentence; a second press has nothing left to do;
-3. a row the older side gets back (an undo) is restored on the copy by the next Copy again;
-4. the owner's Switch back plan after a switch does not put the deleted job back into the older
-   table.
-
-The colour rule is already carried by the attribute pass (CUTOVER-READINESS); it is asserted here so
-the census has every kind proven in one place.
-
-RED before ``moverdeletions_copying_again_carries_what_the_older_side_removed.sql`` (and the mover's
-removal pass): every removal is still live on the copy after Copy again, and no check names it.
-AGAINST THE DEV CLONE (``--records-target clone``), one transaction, rolled back.
-"""
